    <statement><p>Estimate <m>f(1.98,-3.03)</m> given that <m>f(2,-3)=-2, f_x(2,-3)=3</m> and <m>f_y(2,-3)=4</m>.</p>
<p><m>f(1.98,-3.03) \approx</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-2.18</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f</m> at the point <m>(2,-3)</m>, which is
<me>f(2+h,-3+k)\approx f(2,-3)+f_x(2,-3)h+f_y(2,-3)k</me>
Substituting the given values and <m>h=-0.02, k=-0.03</m> we obtain the following approximation
<me>f(1.98,-3.03)\approx -2 + 3 \cdot (-0.02) + 4 \cdot (-0.03)=-2.18</me>





</solution>
